should you start in network marketing so  i got a great question from one of my  youtube viewers love you guys  erica who loves working with people  loves working with parents loves working  with children  and finds that her job is super limiting  and  she's not able to have as big an impact  that she wants to have so she's looking  to get into networking marketing to be  able to quit her job  do network marketing full-time but she's  struggling to achieve her goals  and she asked for my advice on how to  get there so this is a fantastic  question and i have three  bits of advice to help you erica in  making your decision  number one is examine your why why are  you doing this  why are you starting up in the network  marketing industry see a lot of people  starting network marketing because they  think they can make a lot of quick money  right you look at all the websites and  it says  easy way to make an extra thousand  dollars or five thousand dollars or ten  thousand dollars or fifty thousand  dollars a month  and you're unlured by that you wanna  make that extra cash until you sign up  and you typically never get those  results so you have to be doing it for  the right reasons  a lot of people started network  marketing to run away from something  else  you hate your job you hate your city you  hit your family whatever it is you're  running away from something  instead of running towards something and  this is honestly i feel  somewhere that you might be in that gray  zone right now i feel like you're  running away from your job  you feel it's limiting you feel like  you're not getting the potential you  have there and so you're running  towards network marketing as a solution  running away from something  isn't a good enough reason look in  relationships for example  if you're in a relationship with a guy  and you hate it and you got to get out  of it  you don't want to just run away from him  to jump into another relationship to get  away from the first guy  because chances are the new guy isn't  going to work out either instead you  want to design your life on purpose and  run  towards things that support you and if  that means it's network marketing then  by all means  go in for it number two is sell products  you believe in  again so many people jump into network  marketing because they think they can  make tons of money  and they're selling stuff that they have  no product on knowledge or awareness  about  they're selling things that they don't  actually use or actually endorse  how do you expect me to buy something  from you and get excited about it  when you don't actually use it and are  excited about it yourself  whatever business you're in network  marketing or otherwise you need to sell  products and services that you actually  use and love  when you're talking to people i should  feel that passion coming through because  you use that product so much this needs  to be a product or service that you  would recommend to your mother or your  kids to use  erica you said you love working with  parents and kids would you refer  these products to your own parents and  your own kids if you wouldn't then  you'll never have success  with this network marketing company no  matter what strategies people give you  because you don't believe in the product  understanding your why and having a  product that you believe in  are the two most common reasons for  failure  in the network marketing industry if you  solve both of those two then you're  ready for number three  and that's model success you want to  find people who are already doing what  you're doing  really well model their strategies and  apply it to your business  now in a network marketing industry you  should have an upline right you should  have somebody who  recruited you into the business and  somebody recruited them into the  business and ideally you're working with  an upline that is supportive  that gives you training that helps you  it answers your questions that tells you  how they did it  and instead of just recruiting new  people all the time they're actually  concerned about the development of the  people that they bring on  a lot of people have really bad uplines  and you want to make sure that  when you're joining a new opportunity  you have that mentor there to guide you  to help you to become successful  but i'd also take a step beyond that  read books watch videos  learn from successful entrepreneurs who  are in the network marketing business  or otherwise because you can learn from  their strategies  and apply it to make your business  successful starting any kind of business  is hard and to have success you really  need to make sure that you examine your  why  that you sell products and services you  believe in and that you model success  good luck erica and believe for those of  you watching i'd love to hear from you  in the comments your success your  thoughts your opinions on network  marketing i'm going to join in that  discussion with you  and if you like the video you want to  see more don't forget to subscribe to  the channel  thank you so much for watching and i'll  see you soon  i'm calvin moyer i'm a singer songwriter  and radio personality  i subscribed to evan's newsletter a few  years ago  it has really helped me the newsletter  is very informative and inspiring  and it has helped me throughout my  career so i encourage you  to don't give up you can make it  subscribe to evan's newsletter today  you won't regret it  you
 

